// PLAN-875 runtime-camera2d/1 sample: the user configures the Run-owned 2D
// follow camera in app_start (target = this Run bound character, world rect
// x[0,30] y[-4,12], viewport 12x8) and owns every gameplay parameter. The
// host clamps the follow center into the rect and letterboxes the viewport
// (570x380 centered in the 800x380 game child); editing the rect/viewport
// below and re-running is the real config-sensitivity proof (V-02);
// main-alt.at is that edited state kept as a separate file.
var speed=4.0
var jump=8.0
var gravity=20.0
var vy=0.0
var grounded=0
var ok=0
fn app_start() {
 ok=ok+ag_char_bind(1)
 ok=ok+ag_char_solid(2)
 ok=ok+ag_char_solid(3)
 ok=ok+ag_char_solid(4)
 ok=ok+ag_camera_follow_2d(1, 0.0, -4.0, 30.0, 12.0, 12.0, 8.0)
}
fn app_update(dt float) {
 let jp=ag_action_pressed(2)
 if jp==1 {if grounded==1 {vy = jump}}
 vy = vy - gravity*dt
 let hr=ag_action_held(1)
 let hl=ag_action_held(0)
 let dx = (hr - hl)*speed*dt
 let q=ag_char_move(dx,vy*dt,0.002)
 grounded=ag_char_grounded(q)
 if grounded==1 {vy=0.0}
}
